# NOTE: this file was previously UTF-16 encoded and contained one directive,
# `* text=auto`. Git does not parse UTF-16 .gitattributes, so that line was
# never in effect -- confirmed with `git check-attr text -- README.md`, which
# reported "unspecified" rather than "set". It is preserved here as a comment
# rather than re-encoded to UTF-8, because activating it now would newly
# enable repo-wide line-ending normalisation and change the bytes of files
# whose current form the frozen results depend on. Re-enable it deliberately
# if that is wanted; do not do it as a side effect of this file becoming
# readable.
#
# * text=auto

# Pinned data snapshot: keep bytes EXACTLY as fetched.
#
# provenance.json records a sha256 of each file's bytes, and
# src/data/sources/provenance.verify_snapshot() refuses to load a series
# whose hash does not match. Git's LF->CRLF normalisation on a Windows
# checkout would rewrite those bytes and break every hash in a fresh clone --
# turning the reproducibility guarantee into a guaranteed failure. `-text`
# disables the conversion so the committed bytes are the fetched bytes.
data/raw/physical/*.csv -text
data/raw/physical/*.json -text

# Benchmark input: keep bytes EXACTLY as fetched, for the same reason as the
# physical snapshot. provenance_benchmark.json records a sha256 of these bytes;
# LF->CRLF normalisation on a Windows checkout would rewrite them and break the
# verification in a fresh clone.
data/raw/DE.csv -text
data/raw/provenance_benchmark.json -text
